<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kokstad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kokstad is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwazulu-natal">KwaZulu-Natal</a> province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, founded in 1869 at the foot of Mount Currie by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griqua">Griqua</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adam-kok-iii">Adam Kok III</a> and named after him. It was the capital of Griqualand East until the territory was annexed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> in 1879, and it remains a centre of Griqua identity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kokstad.jpg" alt="Kokstad" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A3alb · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kokstad_City_Hall_and_Victorian_Bandstand._(Cast_Iron)._Also_Memorial_to_Cape_Mounted_Riflemen_%26_Volunteers,_East_Griqualand._1899_-1902._03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
